> > 2) my model gives me a warning message that the matrix isn't positive semi definite, and indeed I have eigenvalues just under zero. I still get all the estimates and statistics reported. Is it dangerous to work with the results? The model has decent theoretical backing, I suspect the problem is in part due to small sample size (around 100) and a lot of indicators (around 60, with 5 factors) (note I have no crossloadings in my model). I'm probably doing something idiotic so feel free to chastise if necessary
