> If you have highly reliable indicators (intercorrelations and factor loadings above .8 or .9), then in small samples you can see negative residuals and standardized factor loadings above 1.  Likewise, if your latent variables are highly correlated in the population, then in small samples it is not uncommon to see negative residual latent variances in a structural regression model.  But these are just speculations made without seeing your data, much less knowing the population values you are trying to estimate
