Yves -

With respect to your "too strict" comment - as a novice user, that warning is a good reminder to look at the eigenvalues and see if any are close to 0 or under 0. I would urge you to keep it as it is - your program still outputs the results and it is incumbent on the user to recognize whether it is wise to move forward or not (in the absence of clear guidance from the literature).

